# Architecture boundaries

## Layering

- CLI parser builds `CliOptions`; `cli_request_adapter.py` maps to immutable application requests
- TUI builds application requests directly from `ProjectRef` / controller context
- CLI and TUI call `SpellSyncService` — not core writers directly
- Application layer must not import `CliOptions`, `argparse`, `cli_request_adapter`, or Textual
- `application/requests.py` holds UI-neutral frozen request dataclasses only
- Focused services under `application/services/` own inspection, sync, recovery, setup, diagnostics
- `RuntimeResolver` resolves explicit runtime; no production `ContextVar` for settings or `ResolvedRuntime`
- Core and `project_setup` must not import `spell_sync.application`
- TUI service boundary: see `tui` rule.

## Diagnostics

- Emit typed `TechnicalEvent` / `EventId` through `operation_emitter` — no free-form stage strings
- Presentation copy only at CLI/TUI via `PresentedEvent` / `event_presenter.py`
- Technical log: privacy-safe JSON Lines (`schemaVersion: 1`); user words forbidden in payloads

## Immutability and reports

- Prepared preview objects remain frozen through confirmation and execution
- `ReportScreen` displays results — it does not write history or mutate filesystem state
- Do not add a second implementation of an existing execution path

## Validation

- Run `python3 scripts/check_architecture.py --check` when boundaries change
- Extend architecture tests in the same change

